This variety has codimension 10, and has $48=3\times 2^{5-1}$ components.

+------------------+
|i13 : codimCount N|
|                  |
|         10       |
|o13 = 48t         |
|                  |
|o13 : ZZ[t]       |
+------------------+

Chromatic ideal of a cycle:  Coloring graphs is a classical NP-hard problem,
but it is tractable for certain families of graphs. In particular, coloring the
cycle graph $C_n$ is trivial. However, solving the problem algebraically (see
*note chromaticIdeal: chromaticIdeal,) can be quite challenging using Gr\"obner
bases. On the other hand, this chromatic ideal has a chordal network
representation with less than $3n$ nodes [CP2017]. This network can be found
with the command chordalTria(N), but the calculation requires Maple (see *note
TriangularDecompAlgorithm: (TriangularSets)TriangularDecompAlgorithm,).

