chordalGraph -- chordal completion of a graph
*********************************************

  * Usage: 
        chordalGraph(G)
        chordalGraph(G,ordering)
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: (Graphs)Graph,, 
      * ordering, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, (optional)
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note ChordalGraph: ChordalGraph,, chordal
        graph that contains G as a subgraph

Description
===========

This method finds a simple chordal completion of a given graph G. A chordal
completion is a supergraph of G that is chordal. If a vertex ordering is given,
it completes the graph using this ordering; otherwise it finds one using a
minimum degree ordering heuristic.

+----------------------------------+
|i1 : G = wheelGraph(6)            |
|                                  |
|o1 = Graph{0 => {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}}  |
|           1 => {0, 2, 5}         |
|           2 => {0, 1, 3}         |
|           3 => {0, 2, 4}         |
|           4 => {0, 3, 5}         |
|           5 => {0, 1, 4}         |
|                                  |
|o1 : Graph                        |
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : chordalGraph G               |
|                                  |
|o2 = ChordalGraph{1 => {2, 0, 5} }|
|                  2 => {0, 3, 5}  |
|                  0 => {3, 4, 5}  |
|                  3 => {4, 5}     |
|                  4 => {5}        |
|                  5 => {}         |
|                                  |
|o2 : ChordalGraph                 |
+----------------------------------+
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : G = graph(toList(0..9),{                           |
|         {0,{6,7}},{1,{4,9}},{2,{3,5}},{3,{7,8}},       |
|         {4,{5,8}},{5,{8}},{6,{8,9}},{7,{8}},{8,{9}} });|
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : chordalGraph G                                     |
|                                                        |
|o4 = ChordalGraph{0 => {6, 7}    }                      |
|                  1 => {4, 9}                           |
|                  2 => {3, 5}                           |
|                  3 => {5, 7, 8}                        |
|                  4 => {5, 8, 9}                        |
|                  5 => {7, 8, 9}                        |
|                  6 => {7, 8, 9}                        |
|                  7 => {8, 9}                           |
|                  8 => {9}                              |
|                  9 => {}                               |
|                                                        |
|o4 : ChordalGraph                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------+


Caveat
======

If the input is a digraph, it must be topologically ordered; no check is made.

