codimCount -- codimension counts of the chains of a chordal network
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        codimCount N
  * Inputs:
      * N, an instance of the type *note ChordalNet: ChordalNet,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note GetTable: GetTable, => ..., default value false, get dynamic
        programming table
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, generating function
        of the codimensions of the chains

Description
===========

This method classifies the number of *note chains: ChordalNetChain, of the
network according to its codimension. The output is the generating function of
such counts. For instance, if there are ten chains of codimension 4 and one
chain of codimension 6 the output is $t^6+10t^4$.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : I = adjacentMinorsIdeal(QQ,2,5);|
|                                     |
|o1 : Ideal of QQ[a..j]               |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : N = chordalNet I;               |
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : chordalTria N;                  |
+-------------------------------------+
|i4 : codimCount N                    |
|                                     |
|       6      5     4                |
|o4 = 5t  + 11t  + 5t                 |
|                                     |
|o4 : ZZ[t]                           |
+-------------------------------------+


Caveat
======

