constraintGraph -- constraint graph of a polynomial set
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        constraintGraph I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note graph: (Graphs)Graph,, constraint graph of the generators of I

Description
===========

This method constructs the constraint graph associated to a polynomial set $F =
\{f_1,\dots,f_m\}$. The vertices of this graph are the variables, and there is
an edge connecting two variables iff there is a polynomial that uses both of
them.

+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_0..x_3];                                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal {x_0^2*x_1*x_2 +2*x_1 +1, x_1^2 +x_2, x_1 +x_2, x_2*x_3};|
|                                                                        |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : constraintGraph I                                                  |
|                                                                        |
|o3 = Graph{x  => {x , x }    }                                          |
|            0      1   2                                                |
|           x  => {x , x }                                               |
|            1      0   2                                                |
|           x  => {x , x , x }                                           |
|            2      0   1   3                                            |
|           x  => {x }                                                   |
|            3      2                                                    |
|                                                                        |
|o3 : Graph                                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+


