displayNet -- displays a chordal network using Graphivz
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        displayNet N
        displayNet (label, N)
        displayNet (dotFileName, jpgFileName, label, N)
  * Inputs:
      * N, an instance of the type *note ChordalNet: ChordalNet,
      * label, a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function, (optional)
      * dotFileName, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String, (optional)
      * jpgFileName, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String, (optional)

Description
===========

Displays a chordal network using Graphviz.

The text displayed in each of the nodes can be provided by the optional input
label. The default is label:= net.


Example
-------

Consider the following chordal network. 
+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..e,MonomialOrder=>Lex];    |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal {a*b, b*c, c*d, a*e, d*e};|
|                                         |
|o2 : Ideal of R                          |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i3 : N = chordalNet I;                   |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i4 : chordalTria N;                      |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i5 : topComponents N;                    |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i6 : N                                   |
|                                         |
|o6 = ChordalNet{ a => {a,  }       }     |
|                 b => {b,  , b}          |
|                 c => { , c, c,  }       |
|                 d => {d,  , d}          |
|                 e => { , e}             |
|                                         |
|o6 : ChordalNet                          |
+-----------------------------------------+
The command displayNet N  outputs the following figure. 

chordal network

Caveat
======

If the function does not work, it might be the case that Graphviz is not
installed, or that the package Graphs is not configured. See *note installation
and configuration: installation and configuration,

