installation and configuration -- of the Chordal package
********************************************************

Installation
============

To install *note Chordal: Top, run the following commands in a Macaulay2
terminal:
  * installPackage "Graphs" 
  * installPackage "MapleInterface" 
  * installPackage "TriangularSets" 
  * installPackage "Chordal" 
To verify that the installation was correct, restart and execute the command
check "Chordal".

External Software
=================

The basic functionality of *note Chordal: Top, should work without any
additional programs. However, some of the functions do require external
software.

Graphviz (optional): The visualization of chordal networks depends on Graphviz,
which can be (freely) download from http://www.graphviz.org/Download..php

Maple (optional): The command *note chordalTria: chordalTria, requires Maple
when the ideal is not binomial.

Configuration
=============

Many of the functions of *note Chordal: Top, will work without any
configuration. But some functions depend on the configuration of the
dependencies *note Graphs: (Graphs)Top, and *note MapleInterface:
(MapleInterface)Top,.

Graphs: Visualizing chordal networks requires configuring the Graphviz
executable. The default Graphviz executable "dot" should work, but it if not it
can be changed with:
setDefaultConfiguration("Graphs","DotBinary","myexecutable")

MapleInterface: The default executable "maple" should work, but if not it can
be changed with:
setDefaultConfiguration("MapleInterface","MapleCommand","mymaplecommand")

See also
========

  * *note setDefaultConfiguration: setDefaultConfiguration, -- default
    configuration of a package
  * *note Graphs: (Graphs)Top, -- graphs and directed graphs (digraphs)
  * *note MapleInterface: (MapleInterface)Top, -- interface to Maple
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

