isPrimeSimple(ChordalNet) -- simple primality test of a chordal network
***********************************************************************

  * Function: *note isPrimeSimple: (TriangularSets)isPrimeSimple,
  * Usage: 
        isPrimeSimple N
  * Inputs:
      * N, an instance of the type *note ChordalNet: ChordalNet,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, if the test is positive
        then each chain of N is prime; otherwise, they may or may not be prime

Description
===========

Performs a *note simple test: (TriangularSets)isPrimeSimple, to determine
whether each of the *note chains: ChordalNetChain, of the network defines a
prime ideal.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : I = adjacentMinorsIdeal(QQ,2,5)                   |
|                                                       |
|o1 = ideal (a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, e*h - f*g, g*j - h*i)|
|                                                       |
|o1 : Ideal of QQ[a..j]                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : N = chordalNet I;                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : chordalTria N;                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : topComponents N;                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : N                                                 |
|                                                       |
|o5 = ChordalNet{ a => { , a*d - b*c}                  }|
|                 b => { ,  }                           |
|                 c => {c,  , c*f - d*e}                |
|                 d => {d,  ,  }                        |
|                 e => { , e*h - f*g, e,  , e*h - f*g}  |
|                 f => { ,  , f,  ,  }                  |
|                 g => {g, g*j - h*i, g*j - h*i}        |
|                 h => {h,  ,  }                        |
|                 i => { ,  }                           |
|                 j => { ,  }                           |
|                                                       |
|o5 : ChordalNet                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isPrimeSimple N                                   |
|                                                       |
|o6 = true                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : C = nextChain N                                   |
|                                                       |
|o7 = ChordalNetChain{a => a*d - b*c}                   |
|                     b =>                              |
|                     c => c*f - d*e                    |
|                     d =>                              |
|                     e =>                              |
|                     f =>                              |
|                     g => g                            |
|                     h => h                            |
|                     i =>                              |
|                     j =>                              |
|                                                       |
|o7 : ChordalNetChain                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : isPrimeSimple triaSystem(N,C)                     |
|                                                       |
|o8 = true                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+


See also
========

  * *note isPrimeSimple: (TriangularSets)isPrimeSimple, -- simple primality
    test of triangular systems

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note isPrimeSimple(ChordalNet): isPrimeSimple_lpChordalNet_rp, -- simple
    primality test of a chordal network
