nextChain -- iterates over the chains of a chordal network
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        C = nextChain(N)
        C' = nextChain(C,N)
        (C,data) = nextChain(cdim,N)
        C' = nextChain(C,data,cdim,N)
  * Inputs:
      * N, an instance of the type *note ChordalNet: ChordalNet,, 
      * C, an instance of the type *note ChordalNetChain: ChordalNetChain,, an
        initial chain (optional)
      * cdim, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, codimension of the chain
        (optional)
      * data, a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, cached data from
        previous computations (if codimension is specified)
  * Outputs:
      * C', an instance of the type *note ChordalNetChain: ChordalNetChain,,
        the next chain of the chordal network, if any
      * data, a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, cached data for future
        computations (if codimension is specified)

Description
===========

This method produces the *note chains: ChordalNetChain, of a chordal network
one at a time. It can also iterate only over chains of a specified codimension.

Returns "null" if none.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : I = toLex edgeIdeal cycleGraph 9;             |
|                                                   |
|o1 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x ]                           |
|                  1   9                            |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : N = chordalNet I;                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : chordalTria N;                                |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : codimCount N                                  |
|                                                   |
|      8     7      6     5                         |
|o4 = t  + 9t  + 20t  + 9t                          |
|                                                   |
|o4 : ZZ[t]                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : nC = 0;                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : C = nextChain N;                              |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : while C=!=null do (C=nextChain(C,N); nC=nC+1;)|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : nC                                            |
|                                                   |
|o8 = 39                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------+

We can specify the codimension of the chains.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : nC = 0;                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : (C,data) = nextChain(5,N);                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : while C=!=null do (C=nextChain(C,data,5,N); nC=nC+1;)|
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : nC                                                   |
|                                                           |
|o12 = 9                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+


See also
========

  * *note ChordalNetChain: ChordalNetChain, -- a chain of a chordal network
  * *note codimCount: codimCount, -- codimension counts of the chains of a
    chordal network

