reduceDimension -- removes arcs of a chordal network of small dimension
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        reduceDimension N
  * Inputs:
      * N, an instance of the type *note ChordalNet: ChordalNet,, 
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * no output
  * Consequences:
      * the input chordal network is modified

Description
===========

Reduces a chordal network, by prunning the arcs that do not belong to the top
$k$ dimensional parts of the variety.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..j,MonomialOrder=>Lex];                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal {a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, e*h - f*g, g*j - h*i, a*j - b*i};|
|                                                                       |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : N = chordalNet I;                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : chordalTria N;                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : codimCount N                                                      |
|                                                                       |
|       7      6      5    4                                            |
|o5 = 2t  + 17t  + 14t  + t                                             |
|                                                                       |
|o5 : ZZ[t]                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : reduceDimension(N,2);                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : codimCount N                                                      |
|                                                                       |
|        5    4                                                         |
|o7 = 14t  + t                                                          |
|                                                                       |
|o7 : ZZ[t]                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : reduceDimension(N,1);                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : codimCount N                                                      |
|                                                                       |
|      4                                                                |
|o9 = t                                                                 |
|                                                                       |
|o9 : ZZ[t]                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

The method *note topComponents(ChordalNet): topComponents_lpChordalNet_rp, is
equivalent to reduceDimension(N,1).



Caveat
======

An arc is removed only if all the *note chains: ChordalNetChain, through it
have small dimension. If an arc belongs to a chain of large dimension and a
chain of small dimension, then the arc will not be removed.

See also
========

  * *note codimCount: codimCount, -- codimension counts of the chains of a
    chordal network
  * *note topComponents: (PrimaryDecomposition)topComponents, -- compute top
    dimensional component of an ideal or module

For the programmer
==================

The object *note reduceDimension: reduceDimension, is a *note function closure:
(Macaulay2Doc)FunctionClosure,.

