reduceNet -- reduces a chordal network
**************************************

  * Usage: 
        reduceNet N
  * Inputs:
      * N, an instance of the type *note ChordalNet: ChordalNet,, 
  * Outputs:
      * no output
  * Consequences:
      * the input chordal network is modified

Description
===========

Simplifies a chordal network by applying a sequence of reduction rules (while
preserving the underlying variety).

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : I = adjacentMinorsIdeal(QQ,2,4);|
|                                     |
|o1 : Ideal of QQ[a..h]               |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : N = chordalNet I;               |
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : chordalTria N;                  |
+-------------------------------------+
|i4 : codimCount N                    |
|                                     |
|       5     4     3                 |
|o4 = 2t  + 6t  + 3t                  |
|                                     |
|o4 : ZZ[t]                           |
+-------------------------------------+
|i5 : reduceNet N                     |
+-------------------------------------+
|i6 : codimCount N                    |
|                                     |
|       4     3                       |
|o6 = 5t  + 3t                        |
|                                     |
|o6 : ZZ[t]                           |
+-------------------------------------+


See also
========

  * *note reduceDimension: reduceDimension, -- removes arcs of a chordal
    network of small dimension

Ways to use reduceNet:
======================

  * "reduceNet(ChordalNet)"

For the programmer
==================

