RingElement % ChordalNet -- ideal membership test
*************************************************

  * Operator: *note %: (Macaulay2Doc)%,
  * Usage: 
        f % N
        pseudoRemainder(f,N)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
      * N, an instance of the type *note ChordalNet: ChordalNet,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, random linear
        combination of the pseudo-remainder of f by the chains of N

Description
===========

This method gives a randomized algorithm for ideal membership. If $f$ lies in
the *note saturated ideal: (TriangularSets)saturate_lpTriaSystem_rp, of each of
the *note chains: ChordalNetChain, of the network, then the output is always
zero. Otherwise, it returns a nonzero element with high probability.

As an example, consider the ideal of cyclically adjacent minors.

+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : I = adjacentMinorsIdeal(QQ,2,6);    |
|                                         |
|o1 : Ideal of QQ[a..l]                   |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = gens ring I;                    |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i3 : J = I + (X_0 * X_(-1) - X_1*X_(-2));|
|                                         |
|o3 : Ideal of QQ[a..l]                   |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i4 : f = sum gbList J;                   |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i5 : N = chordalNet J;                   |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i6 : chordalTria N;                      |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i7 : f % N == 0                          |
|                                         |
|o7 = true                                |
+-----------------------------------------+


Caveat
======

It is assumed that the base field has sufficiently many elements. For small
finite fields one must work over a suitable field extension.

See also
========

  * pseudoRemainder(RingElement,RingElement,RingElement) (missing
    documentation)
  * *note pseudoRemainder(RingElement,TriaSystem): (TriangularSets)RingElement
    % TriaSystem, -- pseudo-remainder by a triangular set
  * *note saturate(TriaSystem): (TriangularSets)saturate_lpTriaSystem_rp, --
    saturated ideal of a triangular system

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note RingElement % ChordalNet: RingElement % ChordalNet, -- ideal
    membership test
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

