setDefaultConfiguration -- default configuration of a package
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        setDefaultConfiguration(packge,key,val)
  * Inputs:
      * packge, a *note package: (Macaulay2Doc)Package,, 
      * key, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 
      * val, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 

Description
===========

This function modifies the init file of a package by setting the default value
of key.

The package *note Chordal: Top, does not have any configuration options, but
its dependencies *note Graphs: (Graphs)Top, and *note MapleInterface:
(MapleInterface)Top, do. For instance, the command

setDefaultConfiguration("Graphs","DotBinary","circo")

sets the Graphviz binary used for visualizing graphs and chordal networks.



Caveat
